WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Here's a story, drawn as a ribbon
of tension running across the page.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.580
A door slams.

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.700
A storm.

4
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:08.860
A siren.

5
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.100
A hospital.

6
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.730
Then a house, years later.

7
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.750
More events keep arriving.

8
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.010
The whole ribbon starts to
strain under the weight.

9
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.800
Many exam stories go wrong like this.

10
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.390
But where: the beginning,
the middle, or the end?

11
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.680
In this mission, you'll
put each part on trial.

12
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.710
An opening without enough action?

13
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.930
A middle where too little happens?

14
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.030
The ending?

15
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.670
You'll map stories on a tension graph,
from the first line to the last.

16
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.570
And you'll rank story plans
for a title, The Last Train,

17
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.250
the way an examiner would.

18
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.940
Your mission: work out where
these stories go wrong.
